Thanks for your reply and your wonderful project, @safishamsi. Thanks for your link, @azizur100389. Sorry, this is not a bug of graphify. It might a bug of Claude Code running in PowerShell 5 on Windows 10, instead. I fixed it by installing [Qell](https://github.com/FurbySoup/quell). Here's how:
1. Download qell.exe, the CLI version,  from its releases page, and make it available from your %path% environment variable;
2. Uninstall Claude Code if it was installed with npm: `npm uninstall -g @anthropic-ai/claude-code`;
3. Reinstall Claude Code with `irm https://claude.ai/install.ps1 | iex` or `winget install Anthropic.ClaudeCode`, because the npm version cannot work with Qell;
4. Restart PowerShell and run Claude Code this way: qell claude;
BTW, PowerShell 5 is a built-in version. Installing PowerShell 6 or 7 cannot overwrite 5 and even makes the situation worse with compatibility problems on Windows 10. Surprisingly, there's no vertical scrolling problem with PowerShell 5.1.26100.7920 on my Windows 11 machine.

Please close this issue, @safishamsi . Thanks.

