@maticijus thanks for the detailed Python repro — 14 `cli.py` files collapsing into a single god node is a great example of this issue in the wild.

The fix in PR #441 handles all of these cases. It detects colliding IDs (from any language — C#, Python, JS, Go, etc.) and disambiguates them using progressively deeper path components from the source file. So `insider-flow/cli.py` → `insider_flow_cli_main`, `npt-delta/cli.py` → `npt_delta_cli_main`, etc.

Latest push also fixes an edge case where the renamed ID could shadow an existing node from a different group (reported by @Qodo-Free-For-OSS on the PR).

